his Section Alumni Make a Gift Support Fisher Update Info or Submit Class Note Fisher College Athletics Golf Classic Fundraiser Fisher Blog Corporate Partnerships Title IX Sexual Misconduct Campus Climate Survey News Fisher Today Magazine Faculty and Staff Info Human Resources Accounts Payable Breadcrumb Home / Resources / Faculty and Staff Info Faculty and Staff Info Single Hero This is your central hub for accessing essential tools and information to support your work at Fisher College. Here you'll find quick links and helpful resources related to email and course management, brand guidelines, website requests, human resources information, and much more. In This Section Human Resources Accounts Payable MyFisher Grade maintenance, student lookup, course rosters, and student registration. Email Access your fisher.edu e-mail account. Staff Directory Staff and department directory. Faculty Faculty bios and department. Canvas Access to course management software. Contact Patrick McGovern for support. College Library Library catalog, databases, instructor services. Asana Project and task management request system. Finalsite Login Website content management system (CMS). Additional Resources Emergency Notification System Institutional Review Board (IRB) Brand Book Website Requests The Center for Teaching Excellence Emergency Notification System This form requires Javascript to be enabled for submission and authorization. * Required Emergency Notification System Fisher College has implemented an Emergency Notification System with Everbridge to improve the College's ability to reach students, faculty, and staff with time-sensitive information during unforeseen events or emergencies. The system uses voice calls, email, and text messaging to provide the campus community with pertinent information and details on appropriate responses during critical situations. We encourage all campus community members to take advantage of the opportunity to provide multiple contact options. Notifications will come from the following: Voice notifications: 617-236-8800 SMS text messages: 89361 Email: noreply@everbridge.com The system is initially populated with your name and college email account, but you have the ability to update your personal info on the web at Everbridge or using the Everbridge 360 app. The Everbridge 360 Mobile App is available for download from: Apple App Store Google Play Store When using the mobile app you will need to enter the organization code: fisher118 Everbridge 360 uses Single Sign-On (SSO) via your college email account to log on. If you have any questions, please email DeanofStudents@Fisher.edu and is-team@Fisher.edu IF YOU CANNOT LOGIN TO EVERBRIDGE PLEASE FILL OUT THE FORM BELOW I am a * required Student Faculty/Staff Member Status * required Full Time Part Time Employee Name * required Student Name * required Student ID * required Cell Phone Number * required Alternative E-mail Address * required @fisher.edu email will be your primary e-mail address in our system for FERPA compliance purposes)​ Location * required Select One​​ Boston Campus Brockton Hospital Online Select One​​ Please complete the security verification below. Submit Institutional Review Board (IRB) The Fisher College Institutional Review Board (IRB) is a group of five full time faculty and administrators who serve to oversee and support compliance with federal guidelines for conducting research that involves the use of human subjects. The IRB is responsible for protecting the rights and welfare of human subjects that participate in College related research or research the College has agreed to support. The IRB must review all relevant research through an application process prior to research being conducted. Full procedures and the IRB application can be found at the links below: IRB Application Form IRB Composition and Procedures Brand Book The Fisher College brand book can be used to ensure consistency in messaging and communication across the college, helping faculty and staff represent Fisher College in a unified way. This will be especially helpful for faculty and staff when creating presentations, marketing materials, or social media content. Included in the Brand Book are Fisher College's fonts and colors, plus links to a file of logos for use in Fisher College-related materials. Brand Book Website Requests If you do not have access to Finalsite or Asana, email your website edit requests directly to Colleen Gordon, Digital Content Manager, and include the following information: Include the URL(s) of the page(s) needing updates. Specify if the copy is a \"replacement\" or \"addition\" to existing content. Use quotations for exact wording changes (e.g., \"change 'XYZ' to 'ABC'\"). Specify deadline for updates. Please allow at least 2-3 business days for completion. Attach screenshots for specific placement requests (if possible). If you have resources such as PDFs that need to be replaced, provide the name of the resource that is currently on the website. The Center for Teaching Excellence The Center for Teaching Excellence (CTE) at Fisher College collaborates with all faculty to help guide their on-going professional development as reflective and innovative teachers within a diverse learner-centered institution. In order to best serve the diverse population of Fisher College, we organize our practices around the following objectives: Provide orientation, mentoring and instructional support for all faculty at the college Provide a variety of professional development activities to promote effective teaching and learning practices for a diverse student population. Encourage learner-centered teaching practices that work to foster active and engaged learning environments Assist faculty and students with academic support of the Learning Management System Provide instructional training and assistance for online and blended teaching Enhance and expand collaborative opportunities for students and faculty across disciplines Research, evaluate and provide opportunities for reflection and dialogue about the changing nature of teaching and learning For information or inquires contact CTE Director Heidi Hendershott, Ph.D. hhendershott@fisher.edu Technology Resources Install Office 365 Microsoft Teams Outlook for Android Outlook for iOS OneLogin Password Change Quickstart OneDrive Campus 118 Beacon Street Boston MA 02116 617.236.8800 Connect with Us Facebook (opens in new window/tab) Instagram (opens in new window/tab) TikTok (opens in new window/tab) YouTube (opens in new window/tab) X Fisher College Apply (opens in new window/tab) Quick Links Work with Us Athletics Corporate Partnerships News FAQs Order Transcripts Contact Us Notices and Disclosures Fisher College admits students of any race, color, national and ethnic origin to all the rights, privileges, programs, and activities generally accorded or made available to students at CCES. CCES does not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, national or ethnic origin, creed, religion, or sexual orientation in the administration of its educational policies, admission policies, financial aid, scholarship or other programs, or athletic or other school-administered programs and activities. © Copyright 2001-2026, Fisher College. All rights reserved Site Map Privacy Policy Notices & Disclosures Consent Preferences Powered by Finalsite"
